 "about": [
  "Where fetched code comes from sets the severity of running it (curl | sh, sh -c \"$(curl …)\", bash <(curl …), irm | iex) and of installing a package from a URL (pip install git+…, npx github:…).",
  "Known: an installer below, matched on host + path (lowercase; an entry ending in '/', '.' or '_' is a prefix, any other is the whole path or a folder), or a github.com, raw.githubusercontent.com, codeload.github.com, gitlab.com or bitbucket.org repository of an owner in code_host_owners or of the git remote of the folder the command ran in.",
  "Pinned: the command names the version, by the installer's 'pinned' pattern (matched on the whole command) or, on a code host, a tag, version or commit in the URL.",
  "Unknown: anything else, including plain http://, a URL without https://, a raw IP, a URL built at run time and every host in unknown_hosts.",
  "An installer that cannot be pinned (rustup, Homebrew, sdkman, gcloud) is ranked as unpinned: its code can change between two runs."
 ],
